                        "entry_id": "17fe574e-6d00-353f-8621-0a05d4aa5acf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A gatekeeper; a person who guards a gate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31d73b2c-a4f6-46f3-a5ef-c4d577a4fc66",
                                "sense_id": "bf5d45c8-ce24-3562-b070-816c4c780d04",
                                "text": "The cars built before 1913 had clerestory roofs, after the American style, and also were provided with gates and end vestibule platforms requiring gatemen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68d424ce-803a-4328-8d65-dae15d22b2e5",
                                "sense_id": "bf5d45c8-ce24-3562-b070-816c4c780d04",
                                "text": "The carriages - or cars - had gated platforms at the end, where 'gatemen' stood and controlled the flow of passengers on and off the trains in the absence of automatic doors. […] When each gateman had secured his doors and gate, he rang a bell, then the conductor rang his bell as the signal for the driver to set off."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
